.PP
\f[CR]at_path\f[R] reads a path that selects one value: names and
indexes only.
\f[CR][*]\f[R], \f[CR]..\f[R], a filter and a slice such as
\f[CR][0:2]\f[R] select many values.
Only a read with \f[CR]cbor::nodelist\f[R] as the result reads them, for
example \f[CR]lazy.at_path<Path, cbor::nodelist>()\f[R].
It gives every match as a \f[CR]cbor::lazy\f[R], in a
\f[CR]cbor::nodelist\f[R], and an empty vector when nothing matches.
.PP
In a filter, \f[CR]\(at\f[R] is the current value.
A filter compares with \f[CR]==\f[R], \f[CR]!=\f[R], \f[CR]<\f[R],
\f[CR]<=\f[R], \f[CR]>\f[R] and \f[CR]>=\f[R], and joins tests with
\f[CR]&&\f[R], \f[CR]||\f[R] and \f[CR]!\f[R].
Numbers compare by value and texts by their bytes.
The functions \f[CR]length\f[R], \f[CR]count\f[R] and \f[CR]value\f[R]
of RFC 9535 work.
.PP
An index on a map reads an integer key: \f[CR]$[1]\f[R] reads the key 1
of \f[CR]{1: \(dqx\(dq}\f[R].
COSE (RFC 9052) and other CBOR protocols use integer keys.
.SS 5. Errors
The errors of a path are those of basics.md, section 1.
A program tells a missing field from broken input:
.IP
.EX
\f[B]auto\f[R] const id = cbor::at_path<\(dq$.user.id\(dq, std::int64_t>(bytes);
\f[B]if\f[R] (!id) {
    \f[B]switch\f[R] (id.error()) {
    \f[B]case\f[R] cbor::error::key_not_found:
        use(0);              \f[I]// no id: a default\f[R]
        \f[B]break\f[R];
    \f[B]default\f[R]:
        reject(id.error());  \f[I]// the input is not what the program expects\f[R]
    }
}
.EE
.PP
A path reads the bytes up to its value and no further, so it does not
find a fault after the value.
A list or a map that claims more items than the bytes left gives
\f[CR]too_little_data\f[R] before the path reads an element.
\f[CR]cbor::item_size(bytes)\f[R] checks the whole value and gives its
size in bytes.
.SS 6. What is not supported
.IP \(bu 2
\f[CR]match()\f[R] and \f[CR]search()\f[R]: the library has no regular
expressions.
.IP \(bu 2
Function extensions beyond those of RFC 9535.
.IP \(bu 2
Normalized paths: a \f[CR]nodelist\f[R] gives values, not their places.
.PP
More: every form of \f[CR]at_path\f[R], a path at run time, the full
syntax, keys that are not text, tags, typed arrays, limits and cost are
in advanced/path.md.
